# The runtime production starts, and the only place it is chosen.
#
# The deploy job appends this line to the environment it decrypted from
# secrets/production.env.sops, so the switch reaches the host inside the same
# .env.production.incoming that ops/deploy.sh snapshots before promoting and
# restores on a failed gate. A release that fails rolls the runtime back with
# everything else.
#
# It lives here rather than in SOPS for two reasons. It is not a secret. And
# the production age key is held only by CI, so a switch kept in SOPS is one
# nobody on the team can flip back from a laptop in a hurry. The deploy job
# refuses a release if SOPS defines BOT_ENTRYPOINT as well, so there is never
# a second value to disagree with this one.
#
# Editing this file changes nothing by itself: a merge to main deploys nothing.
# It takes effect at the next vX.Y.Z tag.
#
#   src/telegram-bot.js                 the legacy runtime -- the rollback
#   dist/composition/runtime-entry.js   the NestJS runtime, production from v2.0.0
BOT_ENTRYPOINT=dist/composition/runtime-entry.js
